#### C-4 · REFRESH TOKEN STORED AS PLAIN STRING IN DATABASE

**File:** `server/models/User.model.js`, `server/controllers/auth.controller.js`

The `refreshToken` field stores the raw JWT. If the database is compromised, an attacker can directly inject that token into a cookie and get authenticated. It should be stored as a `sha256` hash — only the raw token is sent to the client.

