#### H-6 · `checkAuth` IN `authStore` CALLS `getMe` TWICE ON COLD START

**File:** `client/src/store/authStore.js`

```js
checkAuth: async () => {
  try {
    const { data } = await authAPI.getMe();    // call 1
    ...
  } catch {
    try {
      await authAPI.refreshToken();
      const { data } = await authAPI.getMe();  // call 2 (unnecessary if getMe uses interceptor)
```

The axios interceptor in `axios.instance.js` already handles 401 → refresh → retry silently. So `checkAuth` will: (1) call `getMe`, (2) if 401, the interceptor silently refreshes and retries — but `authStore` then **also** catches the error and attempts another manual refresh, firing duplicate refresh requests and potentially two simultaneous `POST /auth/refresh-token` calls.

