#### L-1 · `cartStore` — `setCustomer` CALLS `set()` TWICE

```js
setCustomer: (customerId, customerData) => {
  set({ customerId, customerData });
  if (customerData?.accountType === 'monthly_credit') {
    set({ billType: 'monthly_credit', paymentMethod: 'credit' }); // second render
  }
},
```

This triggers two separate re-renders. Merge into one `set()` call.

---

#### L-2 · `App.jsx` — EMPLOYEE ROUTE ALLOWS ADMIN ACCESS BUT ADMIN LAYOUT IS NOT LOADED

```jsx
<Route path="/employee" element={<ProtectedRoute roles={['employee', 'admin']}><EmployeeLayout /></ProtectedRoute>}>
```

Admins can access `/employee` routes wrapped in `EmployeeLayout`, which may have a different sidebar/nav than `AdminLayout`. This is probably intentional (admin can test the employee view), but should be documented.

---

#### L-3 · `ErrorBoundary` HAS NO ERROR REPORTING / LOGGING

`componentDidCatch` only `console.error`. In production, errors should be reported to a service (Sentry, LogRocket, etc.) or at minimum persisted.

---

#### L-4 · `invoiceNumber.js` — COUNTER IS GLOBAL, NOT PER-YEAR

The invoice counter never resets, so numbers go `BPC001, BPC002, ... BPC9999, BPC10000` across all years. Most businesses expect `BPC/2026/001` or an annual reset. Consider adding year to the counter key.

---

#### L-5 · `QueryClient` RETRY SET TO `1` BUT NO `onError` GLOBAL HANDLER

**File:** `client/src/main.jsx`

The `QueryClient` has `retry: 1` but no `onError` callback. Failed queries (e.g., auth errors, network errors) will silently fail with no user notification unless each `useQuery` caller individually handles the error.

---

#### L-6 · `client/src/store/authStore.js` — `checkAuth` DEPENDENCY IN `useEffect`

**File:** `client/src/App.jsx`

```jsx
useEffect(() => { checkAuth(); }, [checkAuth]);
```

`checkAuth` is a function defined inside the Zustand store. Zustand functions are stable references (they don't change), so this won't cause infinite loops — but ESLint will warn. Should either use an empty dependency array or wrap with `useCallback`.

---

#### L-7 · `server/config/db.js` — CONNECTION OPTIONS USE DEPRECATED PARAMETERS

`socketTimeoutMS: 45000` affects all socket reads. For Vercel serverless, the recommended pattern is to reuse existing connections with `mongoose.connection.readyState` checks rather than always calling `mongoose.connect`.

---

#### L-8 · `output.css` IS COMMITTED TO REPOSITORY

**File:** `client/src/output.css` (68 KB)

Generated build artifact should not be in source control. Add `src/output.css` to `.gitignore`.

